  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 229 AM MDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nHigh pressure will remain the dominant feature this weekend,\ndeflecting weather systems into southern Canada. Temperatures\ntoday will recover back into the 50s after starting in the 20s\nacross the state. The ridge will bring even warmer temperatures\non Saturday, with highs west of the divide around 60 degrees,\nwhile areas across central WY reach well into the 60s. Gusty\nsouthwest winds reaching 30 mph will sweep from Rock Springs \nnortheast across Casper into northeast Wyoming. These warmer \nwinds will bring even warmer temperatures across Johnson County\nSaturday, with highs well into the 70s. \n\nA weak cold front is dragged southward late Saturday from a\nweather system crossing southern Canada. This will bring light\nnorth winds back into central WY, bringing high temps back down\ninto the 50s for Sunday. \n\nThe next weather impact into next week depends on placement of\nthe trough dropping down the West Coast. Moisture wrapping\naround the bottom of the trough may feed into southwest WY for\nthe latter half of the week, bringing a chance for showers.\nCurrently models have been leaning away from any significant\nrainfall, and have been delaying the initial arrival of the\nmoisture farther into next week.",
